 "notes": [
  "Parts are unchanged from step 1.",
  "Circuit follows the manual: MIDI pin 5 to digital pin 1 (TX) through a 220 ohm resistor, MIDI pin 4 to +5V through a 220 ohm resistor, MIDI pin 2 to GND.",
  "Breadboard holes are read from the image. The image's top half (rows j-f) is the catalogue's 'b' bank and its bottom half (rows e-a) is the 't' bank. The jack's pin 5 leg is in column 7 and its pin 4 leg is in column 9, each in row g. Each resistor bridges the centre gap from row f to row e of the same column.",
  "The yellow wire (from Arduino pin 1) and the red wire (from 5V) end in row d of columns 7 and 9. Those holes share a strip with the resistor ends.",
  "The black GND wire ends on the jack's centre pin (pin 2) in the image, not in a breadboard hole. I wired it directly to midi1 pin 2.",
  "The Arduino's GND header pin is the digital-side GND next to AREF. I used GND.1 because the image doesn't say which GND index it is.",
  "The image shows pins 5 and 4 on the jack's left and right sides, but the manual's text and the schematic decide the assignment. I put pin 5 on the TX side and pin 4 on the 5V side."
 ],
